Subject: server: take the fd limit from sysconf(_SC_OPEN_MAX) on VMS

The OpenVMS C RTL has no getrlimit()/setrlimit(), so HAVE_GETRLIMIT is
undefined and server.max-fds stayed 0 (only _WIN32 had a default).  The
per-process open file limit on VMS is the FILLM quota, which
sysconf(_SC_OPEN_MAX) reports (probes/r_net2.c: 1000 and 150 on our nodes).
Use it as the default and as the ceiling for a configured server.max-fds,
since the process cannot raise it.

--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -1784,6 +1784,13 @@
 		if (0 == srv->srvconf.max_fds)
 			srv->srvconf.max_fds = 4096;
 	  #endif
+	  #ifdef __VMS
+		/* no getrlimit(); the open file limit is the FILLM quota */
+		long fillm = sysconf(_SC_OPEN_MAX);
+		if (fillm > 0 && (0 == srv->srvconf.max_fds
+		                  || srv->srvconf.max_fds > (unsigned int)fillm))
+			srv->srvconf.max_fds = (unsigned int)fillm;
+	  #endif
 #endif
 	}
 
